- **Why:** The low trailing multiples (P/E 11.7x, EV/EBITDA 6.3x) rest on peak margins that come from metal prices, while ore grades fell in Q1 and Q2 2026. The fact sheet's base fair value is 1,440.45 GBX against a 2,719.00 close. The macro overlay (primary weight) leans moderately bearish because real yields and the dollar are both rising.
- **Scenarios (12 months):** bull 3,900 GBX (20%), base 2,400 GBX (45%), bear 1,440.45 GBX (35%). The macro overlay is why the bear probability is higher.
- **Entry price:** none set. At conviction 2 it isn't required, and the obstacle is the business model and macro, not just the price.
- **What would change the view:** three text-only triggers on production/ore grades, gross margin and ROIC. None has an automatic statistics check, because gross margin (66.5%) and ROIC (65.7%) are already above the trigger levels and would fire at once. So the weekly reviewer has to test them by hand against new filings.
- **Next step:** results are due Oct 20, 2026, three days from now. They are the first chance to test the production and margin triggers.

